  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the biological pathway leading to VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that the compound targets the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is subsequently targeted by Diplotrin A and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate. These intermediates are all linked to VMRC-LCP, indicating a potential cascade of molecular events that culminate in the regulation of VMRC-LCP. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside in modulating the activity of the proteasome, which in turn may influence the function of VMRC-LCP. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound acts as a modulator of a regulatory subunit, which is then targeted by other molecules, ultimately affecting VMRC-LCP. This suggests a complex, multi-step interaction that underscores the importance of the proteasome in the biological process involving VMRC-LCP.",
